module "strata.change"
version 1
; A worked domain, and the change language its declarations generate.
;
; Everything above the line was written. Everything below it was not: it is
; what `GeneratedChanges` derives from the schema of what was written, and the
; foundation refuses to build unless the two agree exactly. It is written out
; here so that a change is an ordinary Strata value a reader can see, encode
; and store, rather than a shape that only exists inside a checker.
;
; `Nat` and `Bit` are declared again rather than imported, because a module
; cannot yet refer to another one. S4 closes that.
data Bit = | On [] | Off []
data Nat = | Zero [] | Succ [pred #1: Nat]
data Doc = | Doc [flag #1: Bit, size #2: Nat]
; ---- generated from the declarations above ----
data DeltaBit = | KeepBit [] | SetBit [to #1: Bit] | AtOn [] | AtOff []
data DeltaNat = | KeepNat [] | SetNat [to #1: Nat] | AtZero [] | AtSucc [pred #1: DeltaNat]
data DeltaDoc = | KeepDoc [] | SetDoc [to #1: Doc] | AtDoc [flag #1: DeltaBit, size #2: DeltaNat]
def example []: Doc = Doc On Zero
def raised []: Doc = Doc Off (Succ Zero)
law DocRoundTrips [d: Doc] = d
